                        <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_859">Headcorn, Kent.
                                Chantry attached to the Lady Chapel</orgName>
                            <p><q>Hunc librum contulit <persName key="person_3974">Willelmus
                                        cleve</persName> nuper Rector ecclesie de clyve Kant' domino
                                        <persName key="person_3973">Willelmo Camyl</persName> huius
                                    cantarie capellano et successoribus suis perpetuis hic devocius
                                    deo officiatur</q>. In a smaller hand, <q>Pro magistro R.
                                    Kent</q>.</p> On W. Cleve, see Emden, BRUO, I 437. The chantry
                            was in Headcorn church of which Mr Robert Kent was co-founder (Emden,
                            BRUO, II, 1037) and W. Camyl first chaplain (instituted 1467).
                                (<title>Registrum Thome Bourgchier, Cantuariensis archiepiscopi,
                                1454-86</title>, Canterbury and York Society 54, p.
                            288).</provenance>
